    <string name="what_shows_where_intro">Every event has one home, so nothing is said twice.</string>
    <string name="what_shows_where_ongoing">Ongoing (a call, timer, stopwatch, music, a Live Update) → the island\'s two slots; more come out as bubbles.</string>
    <string name="what_shows_where_notification">A message or app notification → a card, then a dot, or a name-only flash (your choice under Notifications).</string>
    <string name="what_shows_where_system">A system change (ringer, airplane mode, Do Not Disturb, VPN, USB, headphones, charging) → a short island flash.</string>
    <string name="what_shows_where_privacy">Camera, microphone and screen recording → the green, orange and red dots beside the pill.</string>
    <string name="what_shows_where_time">Time → the status rail when it is on, else the open island. Battery → the rail\'s ring, or the island while charging.</string>
    <string name="island_debug_force_intro">Force dummy live activities, so you can see where they end up. With three or more live, the first is on the main island, the second on its left and the third on its right.</string>
    <string name="island_debug_adjust_intro">Width and position, in dp, added to the island\'s shipped layout. Everything at 0 is that layout.</string>
    <string name="island_debug_numbers_intro">The numbers to give as a default:</string>
    <string name="search_settings">Search settings</string>
    <string name="no_settings_match">No setting matches that.</string>
    <string name="status_grid_intro">The island puts its edges in the gaps between the status bar\'s icons, so it never cuts one in half. The pink lines show where it thinks the gaps are. Move them until every line sits between two icons (or over empty status bar).</string>
